{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:5.115.150","page_type":"section"},"citation":"5.115.150","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.115.150","content_hash":"bfafcd749d6ed48c5f591f2c54aab88a72137174c165e98a524066c66d0634c2","heading":"Flea market promoter – License issuance – Denial – Right to appeal.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.115.150:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.115.150","text":"(a) The City Clerk shall review each license application and shall consult with other City departments, as applicable. The City Clerk, after consultation with the Legal Department, may deny the license application for any of the following:\n(1) Fraud, misrepresentation or any false statement contained in the license application.\n(2) Failure to pay the license fee and/or provide all of the information requested in the license application.\n(3) Operation of the business would violate the zoning code.\n(4) Revocation of a flea market license by the City or another municipality within the two preceding years prior to the date of application.\n(b) Except for a denial based upon subsection (a)(2) of this section, an applicant may appeal the decision to the Council in accordance with TMC 5.05.120 . (Ord. 20039 § 15, 12-6-16.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"d089c6a7-4590-5874-850d-b3be069c4e82"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.115.150","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.115.150","content_hash":"4a36ae7d7c562e8002b2c738aa884dbe14a3dea576aefec761db68436b70bb32","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.115.150:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"